  "body": "## What's new?\n\n3.4 is a compatibility release. About 97% of the 472 F-Droid apps we test now run, up from 85%. On the 169 Play Store apps we test, about 90% run, not counting apps with anti-tamper or fraud protection, which Husk doesn't try to bypass. All of these numbers are from testing on a Mac.\n\n### More Android apps\n- Microsoft Word opens (Excel and PowerPoint share its libraries)\n- Slack, Gmail, Teams, Deezer, Flipboard and Picsart get past the crashes that stopped them\n- More engines and frameworks start: React Native's new architecture, Qt 6 / QML, and apps using JavaScriptCore\n- libGDX and other OpenGL apps draw again (3.3 broke these)\n- Apps that keep secrets in Android's secure key store work better\n- Apps with big bundled databases open\n- UPnP and network discovery apps can start\n- Apps that declare their launch screen in a split APK can start\n\n### Looks better\n- Rounded buttons are proper pills instead of ellipses\n- Toolbars, window backgrounds and more color formats behave like they do on a phone\n\n### Less \"out of memory\"\n- Fewer `OutOfMemoryError: pthread_create` crashes on installs without extended address space\n- Unity games use less address space on sideloaded installs, and keep their frame rate up\n- New in Settings -> Performance: see whether Increased Memory Limit and Extended Address Space are on for your install\n\n### Also\n- Japanese, thanks to @Yuki-1018\n- Fixed Husk crashing when importing a `.p12`, or at launch with one saved on iOS 27 (#220)\n- The Remove and Uninstall dialogs open next to their buttons on iPad (#218)\n- Winlator's Settings page no longer crashes\n- Husk builds with Xcode 27 and the iOS 27 SDK\n\n## Known Issues\n- Without JIT, Minecraft, some Flutter apps and some L\u00d6VE games can fail. Use StikJIT for those for now\n- Browsers (Firefox, Brave, Opera) don't run yet because they need separate helper processes\n- Husk's Java runtime still has no garbage collector, so big apps can run out of memory in long sessions (#191)\n- Touch doesn't work yet in Godot 3 games (#200)\n- Apps with anti-tamper still won't run, and neither will apps that need Google Play services or a Google account\n- Winlator containers don't run\n- Full Android is still slow. Use the translation layer for games\n\n## Thanks\nThanks to @BartolomeoRusso9, @Dey410 and @Yuki-1018 for their pull requests, and to everyone who sent logs. Crash reports are what made this release possible \u2764\ufe0f\n\n## Links\n- Website: https://itslevii.dev\n",
